From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a flick's glide starts before the scroll stop

A page never glided after a two-finger flick. The native scroll stop
went out first, as a zero-distance wheel with an ended phase. The
browser's wheel routing ends its scroll target on an ended phase, and
it sends a fling start only to that target, so the fling that followed
had no page and was dropped.

The fling start now goes first on both paths: the libinput converter on
a tty, and the Wayland event source when nested. The stop native
clients need follows it. A native window still skips the page's
momentum wheels, so it runs only its own glide.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
